    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "I hear you, but you're basically saying highway expansion is just a \"quick fix\" that's fundamentally bad. It feels like you're dismissing the practical reality that a huge portion of the population relies on vehicles for everything. If I'm presenting this to a board, isn't it more accurate to say that highway expansion is an essential part of modern infrastructure, rather than just something that's \"detrimental\"?",
